KG42.register("clusters-a501136c0cea4ad68167c6cb",{"id":"41-data_center_local_markets::v142-d-CL003","paper":"41-data_center_local_markets","label":"CSP offer constraints and local market cost-revenue measurement interface","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL003","label":"CSP offer constraints and local market cost-revenue measurement interface","market_meaning":"Connect the CSP offer, constrained by strict price bounds and by zero net-load and sign branches, to local market cost and revenue calculation. The offer and net load have different local uses in the two chains; expected trading volume participates in amount calculation, but its generation relationship and net-load feasibility have not yet been closed in the supplied chains.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["coordination","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"compatible","scope_explanation":"Both chains belong to the same proposed CSP model under the same regional and temporal indices for offers, net load and cost-revenue measurement, and adopt the same convention of positive for buying and negative for selling. They do not include the operator clearing price in the auction context; the case trading switches also do not automatically become mathematical conditions of these two chains.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The offer constraint and the amount formula form a candidate cluster across coordination and measurement stages through an explicit equal-quantity interface. The local roles of both chains and all original constraints are retained, and the expected quantity is not regarded as confirmed transaction volume; gaps in transaction-volume generation, operational feasibility and measurement interpretation prevent it from becoming a complete transaction decision rule.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"It constrains the strict bounds of the CSP offer and its relationship with net-load direction and zero values, providing the condition of the offer used for measurement."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"It uses the offer, net-load energy and expected trading volume to calculate local market cost or revenue, completing the amount result."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL003-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-price","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-piT","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g02-E08"],"rationale":"The proposed CSP offer for the same region and time period is constrained in R003 and serves as an amount factor in R009. This interface is not an operator clearing-price interface; the quantity term can be zero, and a non-zero same-sign offer cannot be used to infer that there must be a non-zero transaction or revenue."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL003-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-net-load"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-PN"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g02-E07"],"rationale":"Both places refer to the net load of the same IDC and the same time period, used respectively for offer branch selection and for the energy quantity term in the amount. It is a common input; the connection direction does not mean that R003 calculates or generates net load."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-M001","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-price","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-piT"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g02-E07"],"rationale":"The definition, regional-temporal indices and the positive-buying-negative-selling convention jointly support equal-quantity identity, not merely the same sign. The local roles of the constrained offer and the amount factor are retained separately, and the objects are neither merged nor rewritten."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL003-M002","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-net-load","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-PN"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g02-E07"],"rationale":"The source explicitly gives the same IDC net load and the meaning of positive for power shortage and negative for surplus. The offer conditional quantity and the measurement input quantity remain separately bound; a net-load generation formula cannot be added on the basis of the equal-quantity mapping."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G001","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Eq. (6)–(7) for expected trading volume have not entered the supplied chains, and the relevant reference price, reference demand and elasticity parameters have not formed corresponding objects and constraints. The offer cannot determine expected trading volume on its own through the existing chains; the applicable domain of normalization, reference price and the price-difference denominator, and the feasibility of non-negative trading volume, still need to be clarified.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-price","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-ET","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-E02","v141-b-g02-E03","v141-b-g02-E04","v141-b-g02-E07"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should supplement the trading-volume generation relationship, parameter definitions, buying and selling branches and denominator applicability conditions, and check their joint feasibility with the offer constraints and the non-negative trading-volume domain; D only retains the interface references."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G002","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Eq. (12)–(13) for net load and the line capacity constraint Eq. (28) have not become complete objects and constraints in the supplied chains. Sharing net load between the two chains does not mean that its generation relationship or operational feasible region has been established.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-net-load","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-PN","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g02-E07"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should supplement net-load generation and the related operation and line capacity rules and parameter bindings, then check compatibility with the offer and measurement interfaces; this cluster cannot be interpreted as complete energy dispatch or a proof of network feasibility."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G003","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The frozen retail tariff parameter retains the $ unit listed in the source, whereas the offer is in $/kWh and the two are compared within strict price bounds; the dimensions have not yet been clarified, and the parameter values are also not specified in that chain.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-retail-price","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-price","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E18"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually verify the original units, the applicable scope of parameters and the feasibility of the strict price interval; any unit or parameter revision must go back upstream, and D does not rewrite frozen content."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G004","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"R009 uses expected trading volume to calculate model cost or revenue; the source does not explain operator transaction confirmation, actual payment procedures or performance obligations. settlement.payment here can only be interpreted as model amount measurement and cannot yet be equated with a payment obligation after confirmed transaction.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R009::V::settlement.payment","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-ET","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-CDEM","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g02-E08"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually confirm the interpretive boundary of the measurement node; if actual settlement rules are required, sources for transaction-volume confirmation and payment obligations must be supplemented, and expected quantity or CSP offers cannot directly replace transaction volume and the operator clearing price."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL003-G005","category":"unverified_source","description":"The evidence for symbol definitions, offer constraints, trading-volume explanation and the amount formula all remains unverified and has not undergone independent source audit; the equal-quantity mapping and mathematical interface are both candidates.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R009"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-price","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-net-load","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-piT","v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-PN","v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g02-E02","v141-b-g02-E03","v141-b-g02-E04","v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g02-E08"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually verify the definitions, formulas, symbol conventions and applicable conditions, and review the equal-quantity interface in this round; experimental candidate eligibility does not mean that the transcription or downstream scientific content has passed independent review."}]},"rule_refs":["41-data_center_local_markets::v141-c-R003","41-data_center_local_markets::v141-c-R009"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-764575e7d0a5ca80","COMP-a607cc256fbfc1eb"]});
